---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "Write-no-allocate under write-back, timed 1/20: a store miss stalls right after the compare while the store goes to memory, the load of its line then misses and stalls for the fill, and a store hit costs the hit time (cases 9, 2 and 5)."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 0 | Store 0x0A4: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses, cycles | 1 | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
1.3 | stall | timing | - | 1 | The CPU stalls for 20 cycles while the store goes to memory.
1.4 | memWrite | allocatePolicy | memory 0xA4, writearounds, cycles | 21 | Write-no-allocate: 7 goes straight to memory at 0x0A4. The cache is unchanged.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 21 | Load 0x0A4: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
2.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, cycles | 22 | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
2.3 | victim | associativity | - | 22 | Set 2 has one way; the line goes there.
2.4 | stall | timing | - | 22 | The CPU stalls for 20 cycles while memory supplies line 0x0A0.
2.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills, cycles | 42 | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
2.6 | complete | - | r1 | 42 | Read word 1 of way 0 (7) into r1.
3.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 42 | Store 0x0A8: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
3.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, stores, hits, cycles | 43 | Set 2, way 0: valid, and tag 0x01 matches. Hit.
3.3 | write | writePolicy | dirty 2/0, word 2/0/2 | 43 | Write 9 into word 2 of way 0 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x0A8 is now stale.
